{
  "case_id": "2007-06-666",
  "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (C. Christopher Trower)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Kentucky's tax exemption for municipal bond interest paid by Kentucky and its political subdivisions to Kentucky taxpayers treats all private entities the same, and favors only Kentucky and its political subdivisions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 06-666, Department of Revenue of Kentucky v. Davis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (C. Christopher Trower)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 0.7,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "Private activity bonds, a subset of which are conduit bonds, account for approximately 20 percent of all municipal bonds issued."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent (G. Eric Brunstad, Jr.)",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a tax case and that makes a difference. It's not a case about a monopoly, and what's key about that is that Kentucky has not taken over the national municipal bond market."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Fine. Then could it do this? Could it say that if you buy cement from out of State, the answer is no, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUNSTAD: Through a tax, no. And I think the Court's precedent in South-Central --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Brunstad",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BRUNSTAD: I think, Chief Justice Roberts, the analysis that the Court made in the New Energy case is directly on point and addresses this. There the Court said the Commerce Clause does not prohibit all State action designed to give its residents an advantage in the marketplace, but only action of that description in connection with the State's regulation of interstate commerce. Direct subsidies of domestic industry does not ordinarily run afoul of that prohibition; discriminatory taxation does."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We actually have that, Justice Kennedy. Ohio, when it enacted its discriminatory tax scheme here similar to Kentucky's, it basically said: We will tax the bonds of an out-of-State State, unless they do not tax Utah bonds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you find that consistent with the vision of the framers for our national market under the Commerce Clause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2b0d9e6ace36-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We come back to the effect of a tax exemption of this type. It is exactly equivalent to the payment of money by the State, because every dollar of that tax exemption represents a detriment to the State."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2007-06-666",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "2b0d9e6ace362e0e1097a10a2efc797ec7c47e50458c9e56fa236e18114a20bf",
